@page "/privacy"
@layout HomeLayout

<PageMeta Title="Privacy · IzzyBlazor"
          Description="What IzzyBlazor's site, the izzy command and an IzzyBlazor account collect, why, and how to have it removed." />

@* Written from what the code does: this site (SiteApp's cookies, no analytics), the account service (its
   tables, in ../izzyblazor-account/Data/AccountDb.cs) and izzy (login, the yearly-free key, generation offline).
   Change this page when any of those change. *@
<Section Spacing="SectionSpacing.None">
    <article class="site-legal">
        <Heading Level="1">Privacy</Heading>
        <TextBlock Color="Color.Muted">Last updated November 24, 2026</TextBlock>
        <TextBlock Size="TextSize.Lg">
            IzzyBlazor collects as little as it can. You can read the docs and use the components without an account,
            and this site runs no analytics and shows no ads. This page lists what we do keep and why.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">This site</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>
                <strong>Cookies for your settings and forms only.</strong> The site remembers your color scheme, whether examples
                run static or interactive, and the order of the docs sidebar. Pages also set a cookie that protects
                their forms, and one that tells crawlers from readers: a random number that lasts 12 hours and
                isn't logged or tied to you. When you subscribe to the newsletter, a cookie holds the address you typed for two
                minutes, so the page can show it back to you. The others hold nothing about you.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <strong>Server logs.</strong> Like any web server, ours records requests, including IP addresses, to
                keep the site running and to stop abuse. We don't use them to follow what you read.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem><strong>No analytics, ads or trackers.</strong> No other company's script watches your visit.</ListItem>
        </List>

        <Heading Level="2">The components and izzy</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            The components and the code izzy creates never contact us. Nothing checks a license when your app builds
            or runs. izzy creates code on your own machine and contacts the account service only when you run
            <Code>izzy login</Code>, when it renews that sign-in, and when you send feedback.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            <Code>izzy feedback</Code> shows you a post and sends it only when you agree. The post holds what you
            wrote, the command you named, izzy's version, your operating system and your plan. It goes to our public
            discussions on GitHub without your name, your address or your account.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">An account</Heading>
        <TextBlock>If you create an account, we keep:</TextBlock>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>Your email address, your name if you give one, and whether you asked for product news.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                Each machine you sign in with <Code>izzy login</Code>: the machine's name, its operating system, izzy's
                version and when it was last used. The account page lists them, and you can sign any of them out.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>The names of the keys you create for build servers, and when each was last used.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                A log of what happened on your account, such as sign-ins, keys created and feedback posted, so you
                and we can see what was done. Entries are kept for a year.
            </ListItem>
        </List>
        <TextBlock>
            Signing in sets a cookie that keeps you signed in, and a second one that holds your name and email
            address so this site's header can show that you're signed in. Signing out removes both. We don't keep
            a password: you sign in with a link or a code sent to your email address. Asking for one sets a cookie
            for an hour, so the code works only in the browser that asked.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Email</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><strong>Sign-in links and account messages</strong> go to your account's address.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <strong>The IzzyBlazor email.</strong> If you subscribe, we keep your address and which form you used,
                and send the email once a month after you confirm. Every email has a link that unsubscribes you.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <strong>The founding price.</strong> If you reserve it, we keep your address and email you when Pro
                goes on sale.
            </ListItem>
        </List>

        <Heading Level="2">Who else handles it</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            We never sell or share your address. Two companies process data for us: Fly.io hosts this site and the
            account service, and our email provider delivers the messages we send. When Pro goes on sale, a payment
            provider will handle payments, and this page will name it. We won't see or keep your card number.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Removing your data</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>
                Deleting your account, from its settings, removes the account, its machines and keys, and your address
                from every list. Its log entries stay until they are a year old, without your name, your address
                or the names of your machines and keys. Feedback you posted stays public, and nothing links it
                to you anymore. Code you've created stays yours.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>Unsubscribing stops the IzzyBlazor email.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                For a copy of what we hold, or to have something corrected or removed, write to
                <Anchor Href="mailto:privacy@izzyblazor.com">privacy@izzyblazor.com</Anchor>.
            </ListItem>
        </List>

        <Heading Level="2">Changes</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            When what we collect changes, this page changes with it, and the date at the top shows when. If a change
            affects an account you already have, we'll email you first.
        </TextBlock>
    </article>
</Section>
